# Declarative source-of-truth for the Starlink gRPC telemetry pip stack (HEAD).
#
# This lists ONLY the direct third-party pip dependencies imported by the
# Starlink scripts:
#   * scripts/starlink_raw_poller.py         -> grpc (grpcio), starlink_grpc
#   * scripts/merge_starlink_into_telemetry.py -> pandas
# starlink-grpc-tools generated stubs additionally require protobuf at runtime.
#
# NOT pip-managed here:
#   * starlink-grpc-tools itself is VENDORED as a git checkout pinned by
#     STARLINK_GRPC_COMMIT under /opt/manet/vendor/starlink-grpc-tools (see
#     README "Deployment and verification"). Its commit is recorded in the
#     software-manifest, not this file.
#   * The Meshtastic collector stack (meshtastic, pypubsub, pyserial) is a
#     separately reviewed system stack (README) and is out of scope for the
#     Starlink lock.
#
# Version pins below are the intended floor/known-good set. The authoritative,
# hash-pinned artifact is requirements-starlink.lock, which MUST be regenerated
# on the target (aarch64 / Raspberry Pi OS) — see that file's header for the
# exact command. Reconcile these pins against the reviewed software-manifest
# before each deployment.

grpcio==1.62.2
protobuf==4.25.3
pandas==2.2.2
